+#### Storage Options
+
+| Flag | Default | Description |
+|------|---------|-------------|
+| `--object-store <URL>` | none | Keep sedimentree data in an object store instead of `--data-dir`: `s3://bucket/prefix` or `file:///dir`. Also read from `SUBDUCTION_OBJECT_STORE`. |
+
+By default the server stores everything under `--data-dir`. With
+`--object-store`, commits, fragments and blobs live in the bucket and several
+servers can share it; `s3://` takes credentials and endpoint from the `AWS_*`
+environment variables (`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`,
+`AWS_REGION`, `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL`), which is how S3-compatible services are
+addressed. Keyhive state goes in the same bucket, so `--data-dir` is unused;
+`--admin-addr` is not available.
+
